From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] iokit: build the GIC ITS and PCI MSI controller

P1-09 checkpoint 3 gives PCI devices MSI and MSI-X through the GICv3
Interrupt Translation Service (docs/kernel/gic-its.md). IOPCIFamily does
the PCI half, and asks the platform for a messaged interrupt controller;
on Intel and Apple silicon Macs that half is closed. NeoDarwin's:

 - NeoDarwinGICv3ITS (kernel/neodarwin/platform, at iokit/ndplatform):
   the ITS's device and collection tables, its command queue and the
   commands (MAPD, MAPC, MAPTI, INV, INVALL, SYNC, DISCARD);
 - nd_iort.c (kernel/neodarwin/pci, at iokit/ndpci): the MADT's GIC ITS
   structures and the IORT's ID mappings from a requester ID to an ITS
   DeviceID, through an SMMU if there is one;
 - NeoDarwinPCIMSI.cpp: an IOPCIMessagedInterruptController whose vectors
   are LPIs, which the host bridge hands to IOPCIFamily;
 - NeoDarwinPCINVMeTest.cpp: a test driver that makes an NVMe
   controller's MSI-X vector 0 fire (probe score 0, so a real NVMe driver
   wins; it drives only QEMU's NVMe unless nd_pci_nvme_test=1, and
   nd_pci_nvme_test=0 turns it off).

This patch lists the four files, gives the new PCI objects the search
paths of patch 0022 (the controller also the platform header), and adds
the NVMe test driver's personality (IOPCIClassMatch 0x010802).

Rebase-risk: low (appended entries; applies after 0022).
---
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -61,6 +61,12 @@
     "     'IOPCIMatch'      = '0x11e81234';"
     "   },"
     "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NeoDarwinPCINVMeTest;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPCIDevice;"
+    "     'IOPCIClassMatch' = '0x01080200&0xffffff00';"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 0:32;"
+    "   },"
+    "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = IOExclaveProxy;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOService;"
     "     'IOExclaveProxy'  = 1:32;"
--- a/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
+++ b/iokit/conf/Makefile.template
@@ -90,6 +90,13 @@
 	IOACPIPlatformDevice.cpo,$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_PCI) -I$(ND_IOPCI) -I$(ND_PCI)/compat \
 	-I$(SRCROOT)/libkern/ndpthread/compat -I$(ND_ACPI)/include -Wno-deprecated-declarations))
 
+# MSIs through the GIC ITS (patch 0024): the MADT/IORT parser, the messaged
+# interrupt controller and the NVMe MSI-X test see the same headers; the
+# controller also NeoDarwin's platform header, for the GIC and its ITS.
+$(foreach o,nd_iort.o NeoDarwinPCIMSI.cpo NeoDarwinPCINVMeTest.cpo,$(eval $(o)_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(ND_PCI) -I$(ND_IOPCI) \
+	-I$(ND_PCI)/compat -I$(SRCROOT)/libkern/ndpthread/compat -I$(ND_ACPI)/include -Wno-deprecated-declarations))
+NeoDarwinPCIMSI.cpo_CFLAGS_ADD += -I$(SRCROOT)/iokit/ndplatform
+
 #
 # Diagnostic opt-outs.  We need to make this list empty.
 #
--- a/iokit/conf/files.arm64
+++ b/iokit/conf/files.arm64
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 # NeoDarwin generic Arm platform: expert, GICv3, PSCI (kernel/neodarwin/platform)
 iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinPlatformExpert.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinGICv3.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinGICv3ITS.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndplatform/NeoDarwinPSCI.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 
 # NeoDarwin ACPI platform (kernel/neodarwin/acpi): the ACPI platform driver,
@@ -188,6 +189,9 @@
 iokit/ndpci/nd_pci_ecam.c	standard
 iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCIHostBridge.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCIEduTest.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/nd_iort.c	standard
+iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCIMSI.cpp	optional iokitcpp
+iokit/ndpci/NeoDarwinPCINVMeTest.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIBridge.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIConfigurator.cpp	optional iokitcpp
 iokit/ndpci/IOPCIFamily/IOPCIDevice.cpp	optional iokitcpp
